{
 "name": "VSCO2 CE String Sections (music-production build)",
 "comment": "Built from VSCO 2 Community Edition by Versilian Studios (recorded by Sam Gossner and Simon Dalzell; sample cutting by Elan Hickler/Soundemote), CC0 1.0. Source: https://github.com/sgossner/VSCO-2-CE at 440300901dfe9275fd84e0b7763af1f8443ae62e. The violin, viola and cello sections, each over its whole sampled range (violins G3-D6, violas C3-D6, cellos C2-F5; the file names sit an octave under scientific pitch) and mapped at most 4 semitones past its top sample: violins on program 40, violas 41, cellos 42, with sustain on bank 0 (also as one preset per recorded dynamic on banks 16 and up, and as legato presets on banks 32 and up, each take entered past its attack), spiccato on bank 1 and pizzicato on bank 2; tremolo on programs 44, 45 and 46 (bank 0, with dynamic layers). Changes as in the main VSCO build: pitch-checked against file names, small intonation offsets as fineTune, leading silence trimmed, levels matched per layer with set soft-layer offsets, 16-bit TPDF dither, round robins alternated on neighbouring velocities. A bank of its own because the main VSCO bank is near the SF2 limit of 65,535 instrument generators.",
 "copyright": "Source samples CC0 1.0 (Versilian Studios VSCO 2 CE)",
 "target_rms": 0.08,
